    {
     "type": "video",
     "title": "Video: separable verbs",
     "videoId": "Tizr0WwCzFQ",
     "channel": "YourGermanTeacher (Luzi)",
     "start": 44,
     "end": 675,
     "note": "Chapters: 1:10 what they are · 2:30 how they're formed · 3:42 conjugation · 4:32 sentence structure · 6:55 separable prefixes · 8:47 prefixes that never separate · 10:19 prefixes that can do both."
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "title": "How they work",
     "md": "A **prefix** + a verb = a new verb: *kommen* (come) → **an**kommen (arrive). In the infinitive they're one word.\n\nIn a normal sentence the verb goes to position 2 and the **prefix jumps to the very end**:\n\n- ✗ *Ich ankomme in Berlin.*\n- ✓ {de:Ich **komme** in Berlin **an**.}\n- {de:Lisa **kommt** um neun Uhr mit dem Zug in Berlin **an**.}\n\nLuzi's rule: *Das Präfix steht immer am Satzende.* (the prefix is always at the end of the sentence)"
    },
